@* macOS: parametric shapes.
The shapes are pure geometry and have nothing to do with the platform. The port keeps the
whole design of the first part: patches, the inversion used by the inspector and the
tangent frame. Only the vector types change, from |XMFLOAT3| to |simd::float3|. Where a
module did not mention a vector type at all it is reused as it is; the header is a good
example.

<<file:mac/src/Mesh.h>>=
#pragma once
